  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 4.06,
      "end": 13.178,
      "en": "At the start of the twentieth century, only about one in ten of the world's population lived in an urban area.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 13.178,
      "end": 16.34,
      "en": "Today, more than half live in cities.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 21.08,
      "end": 29.96,
      "en": "Urbanization has concentrated opportunities for jobs, education, and medical care, but it has also brought serious problems.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 30.88,
      "end": 37.06,
      "en": "Traffic congestion, the high price of housing, and air pollution are among them.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 37.06,
      "end": 40.12,
      "en": "Tokyo, New York, London, Shanghai.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 41.84,
      "end": 48.66,
      "en": "Each of these major cities of the world faces the limits of population density and infrastructure.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 48.66,
      "end": 56.3,
      "en": "In recent years, each city has begun to attempt a more sustainable form of urban planning.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 57.66,
      "end": 67.08,
      "en": "They are creating more roads for pedestrians and cyclists, restoring green parks, and increasing investment in public transportation.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 68.62,
      "end": 75.16,
      "en": "At the same time, people have started to move from city centers to the suburbs.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 76.86,
      "end": 83.662,
      "en": "With the spread of remote work, the distinction between urban and rural life has become less rigid.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 83.662,
      "end": 86.52,
      "en": "Cities will continue to change their shape.",
      "ja": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 88.18,
      "end": 94.46,
      "en": "What matters is how we design a space in which everyone can live with peace of mind.",
      "ja": ""
    }
  ]
}
